  "id": "Compound::DB00359 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Sulfadiazine is linked to Cyp2c9 through a series of molecular similarities and binding interactions. The evidence suggests that Sulfadiazine, through its structural resemblance to sulfamoxole and sulfaphenazole, shares a common ancestor in the class of sulfonamide anti-infective agents. These compounds, in turn, bind to Cyp2c9, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the cytochrome P450 enzyme. The recurring theme is the structural similarity between Sulfadiazine and its analogs, which are all part of the sulfonamide family, and their shared ability to interact with Cyp2c9. This suggests that the interaction between Sulfadiazine and Cyp2c9 may be mediated through a common structural motif, possibly influencing the enzyme's activity. The evidence supports a pathway where the structural similarity of Sulfadiazine to other sulfonamides leads to their binding to Cyp2c9, highlighting a possible role in drug metabolism.",
